re we help support  some of their research so some of the  work that's being done for atlasing at  the single cell and spatial level  through through the HCA we have a  partnership  um with the Mayo Clinic and OHSU to  develop diagnostics for the geomic  system as well so while the platform  today is an ruo platform obviously you  can imagine with the digital and  Multiplex capability of this system and  as we push further and further towards  Precision medicine that a platform like  this could be applied in a more  regulated setting and so we're currently  exploring what the development of that  would look like with this partnership  with the Mayo Clinic and OHSU and then I  mentioned and we have our breast cancer  Consortium so this is a Consortium of  investigators uh that have gotten  together to come up with best practices  uh and different ways to visualize and  look at breast cancer tissue on the  geomex platform and so that Consortium  has now come together and and they are  publishing those best practices so we're  really excited to see some of the  results coming out of that Consortium  that we've set up around breast cancer  for the genomic system  but in regards to the Leica relationship  and this automation of our protocol and  then as I mentioned it's standard  immunohist chemistry protocols but you  can imagine you know that takes some  time and some expertise to be able to  know how to do your antigen retrieval  and we've got protocols that we can give  to folks so um you know it we we walk  you through those steps  um but it can take some time you're  talking about like about three and a  half uh three plus hours of Hands-On  time to manually you know prepare a  sample and stain it you know anyone  who's done IHC work in the past can  understand you know that that can take  some time  um and so what's nice about the  relationship with with Leica is this  ability to automate that on their bond  RX system we go from about three hours  of Hands-On time